Port patch 0026 - debug cheat: L+R knocks out the opponent's Pokemon (L+R+Z wins the battle)
Why: a requested quality-of-life/debug feature of the port. It is carried out inside the game's own battle code, not by the host poking at memory from outside, so that the game's
normal faint sequence plays and its state machine stays consistent.
How: Port_WatchKnockoutChord (battle_engine_main.c, called at the start of every battle frame, BattleScene_UpdateFrame) looks at the first player's controller:
L and R both held and any of L, R, Z newly pressed arms the cheat, whatever the order the buttons went down in (Z held as well: the "win" variant; a knock-out that is already armed is upgraded when Z joins, never downgraded). The cheat is carried out in Battle_ResolveMonAction
(battle_engine_359F90.c) right after the turn's calculation and before the game's own faint check (Battle_CheckFaintAfterMove): the opponent's active Pokemon gets
current HP 0 (BattleMonRuntime.unk_0C; the HP shown on screen follows it through BattleScene_AnimateDisplayedHpToRuntime) and, for the "win" variant, every other
Pokemon the opponent brought gets HP 0 in the roster (BattleMon.unk_02), which the Battle_CheckAllBroughtFainted_* functions add up. So after the NEXT turn resolves
(the player picks a move as usual) the opponent faints with the normal animation. When no HP animation is pending (the shown HP BattleMon.unk_02 equals the real HP, which is the case after a move that missed, failed or did no damage) the shown HP and its float tracker D_843900A8 are set to 0 too: after such a move the game calls BattleScene_AnimateDisplayedHpToRuntime only once per presentation round (about 50 frames), a step of max HP / 90 each, so the bar would otherwise need over a minute (reported by the user: "drains incredibly slowly" after a miss or a failed effect). After a damaging move the scene animates every frame and the cheat leaves the shown HP alone. It is not applied in the middle of a menu: the state machine of the turn playback is not
meant to be interrupted there.
The opponent is the side whose active Pokemon is not controlled by gPlayer1Controller (state.unk_C8). The host decides whether the cheat is on (__osHostCheatsEnabled:
settings menu / config file, default on) and gets notices (__osHostCheatNotice) to show a message on screen and write the log.
The armed state (sPortCheatPending) is an overlay variable: it starts at zero whenever the battle overlay is loaded, so a cheat armed in one battle cannot fire in the next.
Meaning of the fields was taken from reading the decomp (unk_0C = current HP: BattleScene_AnimateDisplayedHpToRuntime, D_843900A8; unk_28 = maximum HP) and is checked by a
scripted Linux battle (see docs/windows-test-guide.md); the decomp's own names for these fields are still "unk_".

--- a/src/fragments/battle_engine/battle_engine_359F90.c
+++ b/src/fragments/battle_engine/battle_engine_359F90.c
@@ -1811,6 sha256=36e64eed540f2fce79b785d5a4fefe32a4057924d0566a73de3dfcef36469d2f @@
=3
+/* PORT (patch 0026): the debug "knock-out" cheat. BattleScene_UpdateFrame (battle_engine_main.c) arms it when the player presses L+R (+Z); it is carried
+ * out here, at the end of a turn's calculation and before the game checks for fainted Pokemon, so that the game's own faint sequence plays (the HP bar runs
+ * down, "fainted", the next Pokemon or the end of the battle) exactly as after a real knock-out. 0 = nothing armed, 1 = the opponent's active Pokemon
+ * faints, 2 = the whole opposing team is out (the battle is won). Overlay variable: it is zero whenever the battle overlay is loaded. */
+u8 sPortCheatPending;
+extern void __osHostCheatNotice(int what, int applied);
+
+static void Port_ApplyKnockoutCheat(void) {
+    ActivePokemon* foe;
+    s32 i;
+
+    if (sPortCheatPending == 0) {
+        return;
+    }
+    /* the opponent is the side that the first player's controller does not control (the CPU, or the second player) */
+    foe = (sActivePokemon[0]->state.unk_C8 == gPlayer1Controller) ? sActivePokemon[1] : sActivePokemon[0];
+    /* The shown HP (roster HP, BattleMon.unk_02) follows the real HP (runtime.unk_0C) in BattleScene_AnimateDisplayedHpToRuntime, a step of maxHP / 90 per call.
+     * After a move that did damage the scene calls it every frame, so the bar runs down in about a second and a half. After a move that did none (it missed or
+     * failed, or a status move) the scene calls it once per presentation round (about 50 frames), because the real game has nothing to animate there: the bar
+     * would take over a minute. So when no HP animation is pending (the shown HP equals the real HP) the shown HP is set to 0 together with the real HP. */
+    if (foe->teamRoster->pokemonPicked[foe->state.rosterIndex].unk_02 == foe->state.runtime.unk_0C) {
+        foe->teamRoster->pokemonPicked[foe->state.rosterIndex].unk_02 = 0;
+        D_843900A8[BattleScene_GetParticipantSideIndex(foe)] = 0.0f;
+    }
+    foe->state.runtime.unk_0C = 0; // current HP (see BattleScene_AnimateDisplayedHpToRuntime: the shown HP follows this value)
+    if (sPortCheatPending == 2) {
+        for (i = 0; i < foe->teamRoster->numberOfPokemonBrought; i++) {
+            if (i != foe->state.rosterIndex) {
+                foe->teamRoster->pokemonPicked[i].unk_02 = 0; // the others: HP 0 (Battle_CheckAllBroughtFainted_* add these up)
+            }
+        }
+    }
+    __osHostCheatNotice(sPortCheatPending, 1);
+    sPortCheatPending = 0;
+}
+
=3
@@ -1841,6 sha256=7e4c3939fcaabdc036b9ee9a443dfd3cea2b8997e7241c70698058d49526bca2 @@
=3
+    Port_ApplyKnockoutCheat(); // PORT (patch 0026)
=3
--- a/src/fragments/battle_engine/battle_engine_main.c
+++ b/src/fragments/battle_engine/battle_engine_main.c
@@ -393,10 sha256=7b4ac441a618391d25eb7c8d4a771043f9fee6a45b0b87c5a5574861d0208b41 @@
=3
+/* PORT (patch 0026): see Port_ApplyKnockoutCheat in battle_engine_359F90.c. The host says whether the cheat is switched on (settings menu / config file). */
+extern u8 sPortCheatPending;
+extern int __osHostCheatsEnabled(void);
+extern void __osHostCheatNotice(int what, int applied);
+
+static void Port_WatchKnockoutChord(void) {
+    const u16 chord = BTN_L | BTN_R;
+    u8 level;
+
+    if (!__osHostCheatsEnabled()) {
+        return;
+    }
+    /* L and R held, and any of L, R, Z newly pressed this frame (so the order in which the buttons go down does not matter): Z held as well = win the
+     * battle (2), otherwise one knock-out (1). A knock-out that is already armed is upgraded when Z joins the chord, never downgraded. */
+    if (((gPlayer1Controller->buttonDown & chord) == chord) && ((gPlayer1Controller->buttonPressed & (chord | BTN_Z)) != 0)) {
+        level = BTN_IS_DOWN(gPlayer1Controller, BTN_Z) ? 2 : 1;
+        if (level > sPortCheatPending) {
+            sPortCheatPending = level;
+            __osHostCheatNotice(sPortCheatPending, 0);
+        }
+    }
+}
+
=4
+
+    Port_WatchKnockoutChord(); // PORT (patch 0026)
=3
